  31:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   *           + TIM External Clock configuration
  32:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   @verbatim
  33:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   ==============================================================================
  34:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****                       ##### TIMER Generic features #####
  35:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   ==============================================================================
  36:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..] The Timer features include:
  37:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (#) 16-bit up, down, up/down auto-reload counter.
  38:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (#) 16-bit programmable prescaler allowing dividing (also on the fly) the
  39:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            counter clock frequency either by any factor between 1 and 65536.
  40:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (#) Up to 4 independent channels for:
  41:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Input Capture
  42:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Output Compare
  43:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) PWM generation (Edge and Center-aligned Mode)
  44:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) One-pulse mode output
  45:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (#) Synchronization circuit to control the timer with external signals and to interconnect
  46:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             several timers together.
  47:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (#) Supports incremental encoder for positioning purposes
  48:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
  49:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             ##### How to use this driver #####
  50:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   ==============================================================================
  51:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     [..]
  52:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****      (#) Initialize the TIM low level resources by implementing the following functions
  53:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****          depending on the selected feature:
  54:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Time Base : HAL_TIM_Base_MspInit()
  55:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Input Capture : HAL_TIM_IC_MspInit()
  56:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Output Compare : HAL_TIM_OC_MspInit()
  57:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) PWM generation : HAL_TIM_PWM_MspInit()
  58:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) One-pulse mode output : HAL_TIM_OnePulse_MspInit()
  59:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Encoder mode output : HAL_TIM_Encoder_MspInit()
  60:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
  61:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****      (#) Initialize the TIM low level resources :
  62:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****         (##) Enable the TIM interface clock using __HAL_RCC_TIMx_CLK_ENABLE();
  63:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****         (##) TIM pins configuration
  64:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the TIM GPIOs using the following function:
  65:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****              __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENABLE();
  66:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             (+++) Configure these TIM pins in Alternate function mode using HAL_GPIO_Init();
  67:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
  68:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****      (#) The external Clock can be configured, if needed (the default clock is the
  69:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****          internal clock from the APBx), using the following function:
  70:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****          HAL_TIM_ConfigClockSource, the clock configuration should be done before
  71:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****          any start function.
  72:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
  73:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****      (#) Configure the TIM in the desired functioning mode using one of the
  74:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        Initialization function of this driver:
  75:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (++) HAL_TIM_Base_Init: to use the Timer to generate a simple time base
  76:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (++) HAL_TIM_OC_Init, HAL_TIM_OC_ConfigChannel and optionally HAL_TIMEx_OC_ConfigPulseOnComp
  77:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             to use the Timer to generate an Output Compare signal.
  78:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (++) HAL_TIM_PWM_Init and HAL_TIM_PWM_ConfigChannel: to use the Timer to generate a
  79:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             PWM signal.
  80:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (++) HAL_TIM_IC_Init and HAL_TIM_IC_ConfigChannel: to use the Timer to measure an
  81:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             external signal.
  82:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (++) HAL_TIM_OnePulse_Init and HAL_TIM_OnePulse_ConfigChannel: to use the Timer
  83:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****             in One Pulse Mode.
  84:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****        (++) HAL_TIM_Encoder_Init: to use the Timer Encoder Interface.
  85:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
  86:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****      (#) Activate the TIM peripheral using one of the start functions depending from the feature us
  87:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Time Base : HAL_TIM_Base_Start(), HAL_TIM_Base_Start_DMA(), HAL_TIM_Base_Start_IT()
ARM GAS  C:\Users\n11ak\AppData\Local\Temp\ccFW3Mbe.s 			page 3


  88:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Input Capture :  HAL_TIM_IC_Start(), HAL_TIM_IC_Start_DMA(), HAL_TIM_IC_Start_IT()
  89:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Output Compare : HAL_TIM_OC_Start(), HAL_TIM_OC_Start_DMA(), HAL_TIM_OC_Start_IT()
  90:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) PWM generation : HAL_TIM_PWM_Start(), HAL_TIM_PWM_Start_DMA(), HAL_TIM_PWM_Start_IT
  91:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) One-pulse mode output : HAL_TIM_OnePulse_Start(), HAL_TIM_OnePulse_Start_IT()
  92:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****            (++) Encoder mode output : HAL_TIM_Encoder_Start(), HAL_TIM_Encoder_Start_DMA(), HAL_TIM
  93:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
  94:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****      (#) The DMA Burst is managed with the two following functions:
  95:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****          HAL_TIM_DMABurst_WriteStart()
  96:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****          HAL_TIM_DMABurst_ReadStart()
  97:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
  98:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     *** Callback registration ***
  99:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   =============================================
 100:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 101:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 102:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   The compilation define  USE_HAL_TIM_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 103:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 104:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 105:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 106:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   Use Function HAL_TIM_RegisterCallback() to register a callback.
 107:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   HAL_TIM_RegisterCallback() takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 108:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   the Callback ID and a pointer to the user callback function.
 109:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 110:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 111:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   Use function HAL_TIM_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 112:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   weak function.
 113:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   HAL_TIM_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 114:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   and the Callback ID.
 115:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 116:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 117:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   These functions allow to register/unregister following callbacks:
 118:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) Base_MspInitCallback              : TIM Base Msp Init Callback.
 119:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) Base_MspDeInitCallback            : TIM Base Msp DeInit Callback.
 120:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IC_MspInitCallback                : TIM IC Msp Init Callback.
 121:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IC_MspDeInitCallback              : TIM IC Msp DeInit Callback.
 122:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) OC_MspInitCallback                : TIM OC Msp Init Callback.
 123:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) OC_MspDeInitCallback              : TIM OC Msp DeInit Callback.
 124:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PWM_MspInitCallback               : TIM PWM Msp Init Callback.
 125:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PWM_MspDeInitCallback             : TIM PWM Msp DeInit Callback.
 126:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) OnePulse_MspInitCallback          : TIM One Pulse Msp Init Callback.
 127:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) OnePulse_MspDeInitCallback        : TIM One Pulse Msp DeInit Callback.
 128:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) Encoder_MspInitCallback           : TIM Encoder Msp Init Callback.
 129:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) Encoder_MspDeInitCallback         : TIM Encoder Msp DeInit Callback.
 130:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) HallSensor_MspInitCallback        : TIM Hall Sensor Msp Init Callback.
 131:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) HallSensor_MspDeInitCallback      : TIM Hall Sensor Msp DeInit Callback.
 132:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PeriodElapsedCallback             : TIM Period Elapsed Callback.
 133:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PeriodElapsedHalfBlockCpltCallback     : TIM Period Elapsed half block complete Callback.
 134:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) TriggerCallback                   : TIM Trigger Callback.
 135:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) TriggerHalfBlockCpltCallback           : TIM Trigger half block complete Callback.
 136:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IC_CaptureCallback                : TIM Input Capture Callback.
 137:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IC_CaptureHalfBlockCpltCallback        : TIM Input Capture half block complete Callback.
 138:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) OC_DelayElapsedCallback           : TIM Output Compare Delay Elapsed Callback.
 139:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PWM_PulseFinishedCallback         : TIM PWM Pulse Finished Callback.
 140:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) PWM_PulseFinishedHalfBlockCpltCallback : TIM PWM Pulse Finished half block complete Callbac
 141:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback                     : TIM Error Callback.
 142:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) CommutationCallback               : TIM Commutation Callback.
 143:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) CommutationHalfBlockCpltCallback       : TIM Commutation half block complete Callback.
 144:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) BreakCallback                     : TIM Break Callback.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\n11ak\AppData\Local\Temp\ccFW3Mbe.s 			page 4


 145:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) Break2Callback                    : TIM Break2 Callback.
 146:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) EncoderIndexCallback              : TIM Encoder Index Callback.
 147:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) DirectionChangeCallback           : TIM Direction Change Callback
 148:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) IndexErrorCallback                : TIM Index Error Callback.
 149:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     (+) TransitionErrorCallback           : TIM Transition Error Callback
 150:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 151:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 152:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** By default, after the Init and when the state is HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET
 153:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** all interrupt callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 154:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   examples HAL_TIM_TriggerCallback(), HAL_TIM_ErrorCallback().
 155:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 156:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 157:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are reset to the legacy weak
 158:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   functionalities in the Init / DeInit only when these callbacks are null
 159:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   (not registered beforehand). If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the Init / DeInit
 160:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit / MspDeInit callbacks(registered beforehand)
 161:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 162:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 163:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     Callbacks can be registered / unregistered in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY state only.
 164:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     Exception done MspInit / MspDeInit that can be registered / unregistered
 165:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY or HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET state,
 166:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****     thus registered(user) MspInit / DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init / DeInit.
 167:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 168:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****       using HAL_TIM_RegisterCallback() before calling DeInit or Init function.
 169:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 170:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 171:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****       When The compilation define USE_HAL_TIM_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 172:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****       not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
 173:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****       are set to the corresponding weak functions.
 174:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c **** 
 175:../../../../../Drivers/PY32E407_HAL_Driver/Src/py32e407_hal_tim.c ****   @endverbatim
